  "notes": "8 XLR/6.35 mm TRS combo inputs (2 front, 6 rear); LINE/INST switching applies to the front inputs 1-2. MAIN OUT and LINE OUT 3-10 are balanced 6.35 mm TRS; LINE OUT levels are controlled only by the DAW. Two stereo headphone outputs. OPT I/O switch: S/PDIF mode (optical in = ch 9-10) or ADAT mode (optical in = ch 11-18, out = 13-20; coax S/PDIF in 9-10, out 11-12). MIDI IN/OUT 5-pin DIN, USB type B, external power adapter (not listed). Controls from the UMC1820 Quick Start Guide, 'Step 2: Controls': GAIN per input, LINE/INST for the front inputs 1-2, PAD, P+48V for inputs 1-4 and 5-8, IN 1-2/1-8 (inputs heard on the monitor outputs), STEREO/MONO, MONITORING (IN = only direct inputs, MIX, PB 1-2 = only computer playback), DIM, MUTE (cuts MAIN OUT), MAIN OUT level, OPT I/O, PHONES source (1-2 = monitor mix, 3-4 = playback 3-4) and level. Not clear from the guide and checked on the device still: whether PAD exists on inputs 3-8 (shown here only on 1-2, like LINE/INST), and whether each of the two headphone outputs has its own source switch and level (shown here per output). Modelling assumptions: MAIN OUT and PHONES at MIN are silent; DIM and STEREO/MONO do not change the paths; the digital inputs go to the computer only.",
